-- title:
--   One Meas Naimark Column Isometry
-- statement:
--   **The one-measurement Naimark column is an isometry on the input subspace.** For a submeasurement `M`, let `V` be its Naimark column and let `P_in` project onto the auxiliary `none` slice. Then the adjoint product of the column is exactly that input projector:
--
--   $$
--   V^{\dagger}V=P_{\mathrm{in}}.
--   $$
--
--   The equality combines the square-root blocks for the original effects with the square root of the remainder $I-\sum_aM_a$. It certifies that the dilation preserves the original input space while embedding it into the enlarged system.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.oneMeasNaimarkColumn_isometry`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
